      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sicangu"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Sicangu Lakota translates to Burnt Thighs Nation, possibly referring to an incident involving a grass fire on the plains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sicangu"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Many Sicangu people are enrolled citizens of the Rosebud Sioux Tribe and the Lower Brule Sioux Tribe in South Dakota.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sicangu"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Sicangu Heritage Center at Sinte Gleska University serves as a sanctuary for preserving the history and culture of the Oyate.",
